# eoreader6.1 · kernel · turn 017
# Act: CON*  (Connection aimed at Pattern)   Stance: Tracing   Site: Network
#
# CON's third use: tracing whether the SAME kind of relationship holds
# consistently across independent instances — the same claim-shape as
# NUL*, SIG*, and the still-open SEG*, now checked against turn-16's two
# bindings rather than one. Both are "entity → side_a," bound from
# independently-anchored entities (turn-12, turn-13), against the same
# partition (turn-10). Neither binding was inferred from the other.
#
# Unlike gap-002, gap-008, and gap-011, this is earned on the FIRST
# attempt rather than refused-then-superseded — because the two-instance
# material CON needed already existed the moment CON− opened (turn-12 and
# turn-13 having been anchored earlier, for INS*'s sake, not manufactured
# for this). Worth stating plainly: this is not evidence that CON is an
# easier operator than NUL, SIG, SEG, or INS. It is evidence that the
# discipline is about the material's state, not the operator's identity —
# exactly what gap-011's own note claims (three refusals sharing one
# structural cause) predicts when that cause is finally absent.
#
# Earning argument: precondition is turn-16 (two independent bindings of
# the same relationship-kind). Refuted if the two bindings disagreed on
# which side either entity belongs to — checked directly against turn-16:
# both name "side_a," neither contradicts the other.

:turn-17  eot:opens        :turn-16 .
:turn-17  eot:act          eot:CON* .
:turn-17  eot:stance       "Tracing" .
:turn-17  eot:site         "Network" .
:turn-17  eot:traces       :turn-16 .
:turn-17  eot:consistent   true .
:turn-17  eot:witnessed    true .
